{
  "action_id": "rewrite_priority",
  "rationale": "The reported whole-design maximum arrival is 1.73 ns on the request-to-onehot path. With independently mapped fixed blocks, rewrite_mux leaves that critical path unchanged and therefore cannot improve the objective. rewrite_priority directly computes grouped winners, avoiding the baseline encode-then-decode path and offering a plausible timing and area improvement. It preserves highest-bit priority and the zero-request outputs (valid=0, index=0, onehot=1), while leaving mux behavior, including sel 10–15, unchanged. Exact timing improvement and compliance with the 2719.608320 um^2 area cap require candidate mapping results; they are not established by the supplied baseline reports."
}
